{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504462-giovanni-clan-and-the-others","id":1504462,"title":"Giovanni clan and the others.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-05T10:52:15-08:00","id":1504462,"title":"Giovanni clan and the others.","content":"It's a hypothetical situation, very unlikely due to the ways of the Giovanni clan or Hecata if you prefer, but one that I found myself questioning. What would be the clan's attitude, generally or in particular, in the event that any family member was embraced by another clan, such as a brother who became a Malkavian or a cousin who became a Brujah or even a more distant relative than become a Toreador? Or if one of them awakens and becomes a mage, or marries a family member and has a child, becomes a Garou or another shapeshifter, besides that, you can also think the other way around, if any of them decided to join another faction, becoming hunter, or by joining a pack of Garou? What are your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T11:59:26-08:00","id":1504476,"title":"","content":"Its a question I've considered before. A mage is probably going to get embraced to preserve the necromantic progeny. Another clan will probably be distrusted and be a bit of an outsider in both clans. Garou is actually an issue since duncirn are kinfolk and I'd anticipate graphics levels of violence.<br /> <br /> Cool idea for a troubled pc however","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T12:35:40-08:00","id":1504478,"title":"","content":"double post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 03-05-2023, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T12:41:12-08:00","id":1504479,"title":"","content":"To answer that question, you first need to figure out what vampires consider to be the &quot;property&quot; of another, and how they handle those disputes in your chronicle.<br /> <br /> The game doesn't provide us guidance as to the property laws of the Kindred, and that is probably a good thing overall. Players don't want to have to consult some law code. That's not fun. But we do need to apply some commonsense when these issues crop up in game. Ghouls, other retainers, and feeding territories (once sanctioned by the Prince) are probably recognized as property. So would certain kind of backgrounds like Herd. Allies, Contacts, and Influence are probably more in a grey area. That can be hard for outsiders to determine simply because it's not obvious where the lines are. It's more of a &quot;you can own it provided you can keep it&quot; kind of thing. If someone could easily supplant and replace your Influence with hers, how much did you really &quot;own&quot; it? But if you are powerful enough to fight back, then you do and shame on that other vampire for trespassing.<br /> <br /> But what about things that aren't traits on a character sheet like someone's family? I imagine a Kindred's immediate family and other close relatives are probably seen as their &quot;property&quot; (at least for neonates who still have them). Other vampires would naturally expect you to be hostile if they feed or kill on your close relatives. But extended family probably would not be. But what about situations like Ventrue embracing exclusively through their own mortal family line and the Giovanni? Because these vampires are actively &quot;cultivating&quot; these &quot;resources&quot;, the greater Kindred community probably recognizes the vampires in question see this as their possession and find it reasonable they don't want trespassers. Everyone knows if you trespass here, there is going to be blowback and other Kindred will see you, and not them, as the troublemakers.<br /> <br /> So I think the determining factors here are 1) to what extent is the vampire exercising some time and effort to cultivate or protect this resource, and 2) are the claims of the vampire seen as reasonable to others?<br /> <br /> So if a Giovanni neonate has a sister, that is probably clearly his property. Avoid it. But what if you &quot;abandon&quot; your property by moving to another domain and leaving your family behind? Then your sister might be open to others. After all, if you wanted to protect her you would have found a way to take her with you or stayed local. What about some Giovanni elder who has a distant relative descended from his (long dead) sister he is vaguely aware of at times, but has done absolutely nothing to stay in contact with? It might be fair game if a Brujah embraces that mortal especially if that relative is not involved in the &quot;family business&quot; but just doing his own thing.<br /> <br /> I imagine that some of this was discussed and covered in the original Promise of 1528 which provided some agreed guidelines to both the Giovanni and Camarilla so as to prevent the most predictable conflicts.<br /> <br /> Of course, this implies that Kindred recognize these kind of things as being property, and everyone agrees on a commonly agreed set rules. But I think that is a fair assumption. The Sabbat wouldn't care about this as they're at war with everyone. If they chose to observe such etiquette, it's for tactical reasons. But for those clans who work in a Camarilla imposed framework, this is probably a lot of customary law with the occasional ruling of a Conclave.<br /> <br /> But groups like Mages, Garou, etc. wouldn't recognize Kindred &quot;law&quot; in this respect. At most it is a question whether going for it is worth the hazard of provoking one or more vampires. If for whatever strange reason some Giovanni family member had a First Change, the Garou would want that cub and indoctrinate it in their tribe. At that point it's really a question if the Giovanni in question wants to go to war with such an opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T12:44:07-08:00","id":1504481,"title":"","content":"Right, got flagged by that stupid spam thing, so let's try take 2:<br /> <br /> So, my take on it:<br /> Giovanni are not permitted loyalties that would endanger their loyalty to the clan (such as that Milliner in the clanbook who caused trouble by getting ghouled by an outsider, which was taken as a mark against him and his bloodline).<br /> I think most kindred know better than to intentionally embrace one of the Family. The Family don't like it, and the other clans don't want the headache of smoothing over diplomatic relations with a bunch of outraged uppity necromancers who can fill their havens with vengeful ghosts. It's a political nightmare best avoided.<br /> <br /> But what's most important is that a member of the family is useful, and loyal. Waste not, want not: necromancy is all about recycling.<br /> <br /> But, on the off chance it does happen, getting embraced by an outsider does not guarantee<i> loyalty</i> to that clan. They may not be totally trustworthy now, but hey, that's what the blood bond is for. They bring new disciplines and avenues to the arsenal. Nobody expects that charming Toreador socialite to be a loyal member of the Giovanni family. Player wise, it's also one of the few justifications I'd allow for a pc to know necromancy out-of-clan.<br /> <br /> The Weng and della Passaglia, especially with the family habits that are Yomi-worthy, are not unlikely to produce Hungry Dead. There's a political disaster for the Eastern bloodlines and the Quincunx. Assuming the rest of the <i>wan gui</i> will deal with them at all and there isn't some mutual agreement to destroy members of the family who are found to have taken the second breath. It would make for an interesting character though: enlightenment or family piety? Can KotE's vampires be blood bound? I don't remember.<br /> <br /> Mages are tricky, what with being very strong willed individuals, but still blood bond-able and there's a chance the family indoctrination they were raised with will hold. Assuming they don't destroy the house with paradox, get rescued by other mages or go nephandi, they could be a very useful tool. Probably easier to kill them, though.<br /> <br /> Regular kinfolk aside (and I would hope that the tribes most likely to have kin in the same marriage circles as the Giovanni would know to prevent such marriages), the Dunsirn <i>are</i> kinfolk, likely to the White Howlers. I imagine the various branches of the family intermarry frequently enough, so you could have a kinfolk with the surname Giovanni or St John or whatever. Generally, the first change involves the youth trashing the house and disappearing into the wilds never to be seen again. But the Giovanni do have dealings with the BSDs (who are very complimentary of the Family's corruption). A Giovanni/BSD intermarriage sounds <i>so</i> beautiful. So I suppose you could have some family members in that delightful camp who are still in contact, but lupines are... not safe to keep around. I'd default to <i>&quot;fetch me something lethally pointy and made of silver.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Members of the family who become wraiths, naturally, are still part of the family and expected to pull their weight, often by climbing the Hierarchy and pulling strings for them over there. As of V20 there's a cloud database with the entire family tree in it, covering what state everyone's in (mortal, ghoul, vampire, wraith) and what they're doing.<br /> <br /> A Giovanni kid who goes through their chrysalis? Well, uh, I think a better term for that is Changeling: the Nightmare. If they're useful, and none of the other fey manage to save them, there's probably no reason to do anything to them, though the tendency of elders to rack up banality is going to be painful. Could there be Maeghar Giovanni?<br /> <br /> Being a hunter is a good way to die, Imbued or no. I'd imagine the messengers to know better than to try that one.<br /> <br /> Whether one of the Fallen would stick around if they woke up in the body of a family member would probably depend on if they could see a use in the family's plan. Otherwise they'd leave if they wanted to, and I don't think there's a whole lot the Giovanni can do about that scenario.<br /> <br /> Defectors and &quot;loose canons&quot; will typically be dragged home, re-educated via dominate, and blood bonded, and punished as an example. If they're not very valuable, and nobody of import would be upset, they're likely to just be killed in a manner that sets an example for the rest of the family who might be thinking of treason.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T13:29:02-08:00","id":1504484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504462-giovanni-clan-and-the-others?p=1504479#post1504479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But what about things that aren't traits on a character sheet like someone's family? I imagine a Kindred's immediate family and other close relatives are probably seen as their &quot;property&quot; (at least for neonates who still have them). Other vampires would naturally expect you to be hostile if they feed or kill on your close relatives. But extended family probably would not be. But what about situations like Ventrue embracing exclusively through their own mortal family line and the Giovanni? Because these vampires are actively &quot;cultivating&quot; these &quot;resources&quot;, the greater Kindred community probably recognizes the vampires in question see this as their possession and find it reasonable they don't want trespassers. Everyone knows if you trespass here, there is going to be blowback and other Kindred will see you, and not them, as the troublemakers.<br /> <br /> So I think the determining factors here are 1) to what extent is the vampire exercising some time and effort to cultivate or protect this resource, and 2) are the claims of the vampire seen as reasonable to others?<br /> <br /> So if a Giovanni neonate has a sister, that is probably clearly his property. Avoid it. But what if you &quot;abandon&quot; your property by moving to another domain and leaving your family behind? Then your sister might be open to others. After all, if you wanted to protect her you would have found a way to take her with you or stayed local. What about some Giovanni elder who has a distant relative descended from his (long dead) sister he is vaguely aware of at times, but has done absolutely nothing to stay in contact with? It might be fair game if a Brujah embraces that mortal especially if that relative is not involved in the &quot;family business&quot; but just doing his own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case I thought of a scenario where the relative in question was intended to be part of the clan, but was not embraced and as the clan cannot guard them 24/7 and they do not come with a sign saying that they belong to the Giovanni, you you know how it is, like if the relative met a kindred without knowing it and was embraced or even if it was a life or death situation, or he joined the Camarilla or the Anarchy and did what he shouldn't and now seeks refuge with the family, I think in the first cases the kindred responsible would be hunted down and destroyed if it didn't prove too difficult, whereas in the case if he did run from the Camarilla I'm kind of in doubt, partly because he could be more trouble than he's worth or he may have information from within the Camarilla that the Giovanni can use.<br /> <br /> In the case when I write about the Giovanni I think of them having very strong family ties or operating in order to help the family members until it proves not worth it.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504462-giovanni-clan-and-the-others?p=1504479#post1504479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But groups like Mages, Garou, etc. wouldn't recognize Kindred &quot;law&quot; in this respect. At most it is a question whether going for it is worth the hazard of provoking one or more vampires. If for whatever strange reason some Giovanni family member had a First Change, the Garou would want that cub and indoctrinate it in their tribe. At that point it's really a question if the Giovanni in question wants to go to war with such an opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds plausible. It made me think of the following background, one of the Giovanni's teenagers presents the first change and the family finds out about it and they bring the child so they can try to &quot;cure&quot; her, even to put the plot of a conclave in the middle, then the child is discovered by the Dies Ultima or Wise Guys, maybe both and it starts a conflict, it would be fun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T10:08:47-08:00","id":1504604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the event that any family member was embraced by another clan, such as a brother who became a Malkavian or a cousin who became a Brujah or even a more distant relative than become a Toreador,</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I think there would be a city fight about it (maybe something along the lines of a tradition break) for the party involved in embracing a Giovanni. Think about it like this, lets say that you are a vampire that wants to embrace, now you could embrace without permission (if its a cammie city and you need permission) and suffer the blow out from that or you'd do your research and found they had Giovanni connects and decided they are not to be embraced. For those areas controlled that don't need permission, the party involved is probably just going to die and the Giovanni in question just shuffled into the family.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or if one of them awakens and becomes a mage,</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage is interesting. I think they are likely to be embraced just to save the magical knowledge but, I also see them left alone just to do their own thing and maybe make a more &quot;potent&quot; line of Giovanni necromancers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">or marries a family member and has a child, becomes a Garou or another shapeshifter,</div> </div> </div> </div>I know there is a canon Giovanni Abomination so they are not to shy about having shifters and kin be Giovanni first and their sect second.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if any of them decided to join another faction, becoming hunter, or by joining a pack of Garou?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think really that's what breaks down here. It's not that they are 'joining another faction' exactly they are always Giovanni first and whatever flavor of supernatural they are comes second to make sure the family is strong and has more power.\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T23:44:41-08:00","id":1504732,"title":"","content":"I think the giovanni are going to embrace any mages working under the logic the clan started out as human necromancers, they'd most likely presume any mage was simply a progeny of merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}